From: tcmay@netcom.com (Timothy C. May)
Subject: ECON: digicash?

A follow-up point to the post I just made on digital cash:

* What stops attempts to _randomly guess_ the numbers that make up
digital cash?

Setting even a minuscule fee to "submit" a number for possible cashing
will halt such random guessing. For 20-digit numbers, there are 10^20
of these numbers. A fee of even one cent per number submitted would
imply about $10^18 to "guess" (forge) a number. And the transaction
fees are likely to be a bit higher, at least for a while.


There's a lot more to debate, and anyone interested should probably
get on the Cypherpunks list.

-Tim May


