I basically agree with Perry (wow!), but I think these numbers need some
work. I know the semantics are loose, but I think, from the context, I
get the jist of what Perry means by "enlightened", and I don't even think
the numbers approach 50K. I'd shoot this number down hard by simply removing
all of the transient anarchocapitalists. You know the types, the college
students (not implying all) who enjoy speaking out against the government,
get involved in all these neat technologies, and who then end up becoming
lawyers and government-contract engineers and the like, join the Republican
party, and so forth. I honestly feel that a _large_ number of "us" are like
this, in that, in a few years, they'll forget all about objectivism or
extropianism or anarcho-capitalism, and they'll just be replaced by more
like them. They certainly have their place, but I think the real advances
are made by the ones who stick with this stuff for many years.

Next, I do agree that the government outnumbers "us", but not by very much,
since you'd have to just count those in government who are actually willing
and capable and desire to keep us down. Given the ability of the government
to coordinate, I don't really think you're talking about more than the
legislative branch, the FBI, and whatever other little pockets exist for
this purpose? The military? I don't think you can count them. They only come
in handy when you're talking riots, and I don't think anyone is talking
about taking physical action here.

